  words:
  - orthoptera
  - orthopteras
  info: 'Orthoptera is an order of insects that includes crickets, grasshoppers,
    and locusts. They are well known for producing sound, called stridulation, by
    rubbing specialized ridged parts of their wings or legs together. Most Orthoptera
    species have strong hind legs adapted for jumping, and many also have wings for
    flying.


    Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orthoptera '
  image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 893bd58607b37834daa4a00716025671, type: 3}
